2026-04-23 02:05:57,927 - INFO - ('Translating from English to Vietnamese: The Importance of Learning English in Today’s World\nIn the modern era, English has become more than just a language; it is a global tool for communication, education, and professional success. With over 1.5 billion people speaking English worldwide, it serves as a bridge connecting cultures, economies, and ideas. For students, mastering English opens doors to international scholarships, access to scientific research, and opportunities to study abroad. For professionals, it provides a competitive edge in multinational companies where English is often the working language. Beyond academics and careers, English also enriches personal life by allowing individuals to enjoy literature, films, and music from around the world. In tourism, English acts as a universal medium, helping travelers navigate foreign countries with ease. Moreover, in the digital age, most online content is produced in English, making it essential for anyone who wants to stay informed and connected. While learning English can be challenging, the rewards are immense. It requires patience, practice, and persistence, but the effort pays off in countless ways. Ultimately, English is not just a language; it is a passport to global citizenship. By learning it, individuals gain access to knowledge, opportunities, and friendships that transcend borders. In this interconnected world, English is the key to unlocking both personal growth and collective progress.\n',)
