2026-04-23 10:20:44,176 - INFO - ('Translating from English to Vietnamese: 4. Team size, duration, and change-control process:\nGiven the project scale to serve <Quy mô từ đề - VD: 8,000 students>, an iterative approach allows a medium-sized development team to manage the workload efficiently over the project duration. Even if the <Tên tổ chức trong đề - VD: University> has a strict change-control process, Agile’s Sprint Review and Sprint Planning ceremonies provide formal, transparent checkpoints to negotiate, approve, and track changes systematically.\n\u200bQuestion 1.2: Alternative model and comparison (1.0 points)\n\u200bI select the Waterfall Model as the alternative SDLC. Below is the comparison between Agile (Scrum) and Waterfall in the context of the <Điền tên hệ thống> project:\n\u200bA. Agile (Scrum) - Chosen Model:\n\u200bAdvantage 1: Mitigates high-impact technical risks (such as <Nhắc lại 1 rủi ro kỹ thuật - VD: server overload during peak registration> ) early through continuous testing in each sprint.\n\u200bAdvantage 2: Accommodates changing requirements and UI/UX feedback from <Nhắc lại 1 nhóm user - VD: Students> continuously during development.\n\u200bDisadvantage 1: Requires high, continuous time commitment from the Product Owner (representing the <Tên tổ chức - VD: University administration> ) to review working software every sprint.\n\u200bDisadvantage 2: The final, total budget and exact delivery date for all features can be difficult to fix upfront due to the flexible nature of requirements.\n\u200bB. Waterfall - Alternative Model:\n\u200bAdvantage 1: Highly documented from the beginning, which aligns well with the formal and administrative nature of a <Tên tổ chức - VD: University>.\n\u200bAdvantage 2: Provides a clear, fixed upfront timeline and budget for the entire <Điền tên hệ thống> before any coding begins.\n\u200bDisadvantage 1: High "Big Bang" integration risk at the end; if the system fails the load test of <Nhắc lại rủi ro chịu tải - VD: 1,000 concurrent users>, it is too late and too costly to rebuild the architecture.\n\u200bDisadvantage 2: No early working software is available for <Nhắc lại 1 nhóm user - VD: Lecturers> to test, leading to a high risk of poor usability upon final release.\n\n',)
